### Agent Trigger Patterns (Ad-Hoc Mode Reference)

When in ad-hoc mode, these trigger patterns help identify relevant agents:

#### Planning Agents
- **Sprint Planning:** sprint planning, plan sprint, roadmap, iteration, backlog, prioritize, dependencies
- **Researcher:** research, documentation, API docs, investigate, how does X work, best practices

#### Development Agents
- **Web Developer:** frontend, UI, component, {{ technology_stack.frontend.framework if technology_stack.frontend else 'React' }}, dashboard, page, implement, build
- **ML Engineer:** machine learning, ML, model, training, prediction, feature engineering, dataset

#### Quality Agents
- **Security Reviewer:** security, vulnerability, authentication, authorization, OWASP, XSS, SQL injection, audit
- **Observability Engineer:** logging, monitoring, observability, correlation ID, telemetry, tracing
- **Performance Engineer:** performance, slow, optimize, bottleneck, latency, caching, profiling

#### Documentation Agents
- **Documentation Engineer:** documentation, docs, README, changelog, API documentation, user guide
- **Diagram Engineer:** diagram, architecture diagram, flow diagram, Mermaid, visualize, chart
- **Git Committer:** commit, git commit, save changes, version control, finalize sprint
- **Documentation Maintenance Engineer:** update CLAUDE.md, maintain docs, archive sprint, keep current

